  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\n\nHigh pressure remains south of New England today, with a weak \nfront approaching from the north. Temps peak today, with highs \npushing into the upper 60s, and even low 70s in a few spots \nacross the south.\n\nThe weak front crosses through during the day today, bringing \nonly the chance for a few showers across the north, and a band \nof clouds elsewhere. Otherwise, the front merely serves to usher\nin the next ridge of high pressure, which brings a cooler \nCanadian airmass with it. Highs fall back into the 40s and 50s \nfor Tuesday and Wednesday, but then moderate back into the 60s \nagain for late in the week as the high moves offshore, with some\n70s possible again on Friday.\n\nThe next front likely crosses through during the day on Friday,\nand has the chance to bring a few showers to the area, but \nnothing of significance. Behind this front, the next ridge of \nhigh pressure arrives just in time for the weekend. The next \nridge doesn't look to bring much of a cool down with more of a \nzonal flow pattern, so 60s look more likely for Halloween \nweekend at this point.",
